{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790334664,"nonce":"rK2CF0/vB1BeM/Hu3yPZAcmiASk=","title":"A loop with an inlined call's guard before it has no loop entry, and runs interpreted","message":"bench/ash/free_call.wren takes ~7 s (ash runs it in well under 1 s).\nWLIFT_TIER_STATS shows run() entered once, interpreted, and never\nagain: its 100M-iteration loop never leaves the interpreter, calling\nthe compiled step(_,_) every iteration. WLIFT_OSR_TRACE:\n\n    osr-trace: skip wlift_run__ bb1 unsupported live-in layout\n    osr-trace: no entry FuncId(2) bb1          (33,547x on a 2M run)\n\nrun()'s compiles inline `Bench.step(sum, i)` behind\n`v50 = object_is v14, \u003cBench\u003e` with `v14 = get_module_var @Bench`,\nboth placed in the loop's preheader. A loop entry must either receive\neach live-in from the interpreter as a boxed register or recompute\nit; v14 is recomputable (a preheader read the loop never writes), but\nv50 is a raw bool with no interpreter register and was not, so the\nheader the interpreter's back-edge targets got no entry at all. Every\nloop whose preheader holds an inlined call's class, object or function\ntest on a module variable is affected.\n\nFound on the way: the Cranelift backend emitted every recomputed value\nat the function's entry, shared by all paths, and skipped the body's\nown definition. For constants that is fine; for the module-variable\nread added in 28c5853 it means the normal entry reads the variable at\nfunction entry instead of at the preheader, so a write between the\ntwo would be missed. No reproducer found (store-to-load forwarding\nhides the simple cases), but the placement is wrong by construction.\nThe LLVM backend already recomputes per entry, into the value's slot.\n\nFix: recompute tests (class_is, object_is, closure_fn_is) of a\nrecomputed read; compute non-constant recomputed values in each entry\nprologue, reads before the tests on them, through the entry\nvariables, leaving the body's definitions where they are.","files":null}]}